    description: "iter-002 validation of INV-hunup found 4 non-canonical stable_id producers beyond WI-rijup's 9 doc analyzers; close them all hash-to-canonical (investigation wf_c26241d9-384 confirmed: stable_id is a foreign key with a HARD per-file uniqueness check, unlike fingerprint; 18+/20 producers already hash; the make_synthetic_symbol_identity chokepoint already exists for this case). FIX per producer: (1) sparql.py (3 sites) + (2) kdl.py -- stable_id=symbol_id over a raw composite; migrate to make_doc_stable_id (the WI-rijup fix; first-party doc analyzers, missed by WI-rijup's grep). (3) graphql-linker linkers/graphql.py:223 -- stable_id=call.operation_name on a Class-B protocol_origin=graphql synthetic node; route through the existing make_synthetic_symbol_identity chokepoint (emit stable_id=None to let populate_synthetic_class_b_identity stamp it, or call it directly). This ALSO fixes a latent collision bug: bare operation_name repeats across files -> stable_id collisions, exactly the 'wrong, colliding value' the chokepoint docstring warns about. (4) scip/index.py:203 -- stable_id=sym_info.symbol (real-language node, already has a canonical id via make_symbol_id); hash the SCIP moniker to sha256:16hex (the moniker stays in meta[scip_symbol]). Leaves INV-hunup universal (no language=None exemption -- scip is NOT language=None). After merge: re-validate via iter-003 to confirm 0 nonconforming across the cohort, then INV-hunup -> satisfied."  # 970c
